# Ghost.md: how git treats a library's files (the Back up to git plugin writes this as .gitattributes).
#
# The notes, their version histories and the canvases are text with LF endings on every platform, so a checkout on
# Windows and a commit from a Mac hold the same bytes and a line ending is never a change. The sidecars under .glyph/
# are text with the platform's endings. The attachments under image/, file/, video/ and recordings/ are binary: never
# a text merge, never a line-ending conversion of a WAV.
*.md text eol=lf
*.versions text eol=lf
*.canvas text eol=lf
*.json text
*.wav binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
